{"title":"Positive difference","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The positive difference of two numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> is defined to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/3311eba472bf7dc846f58d649d3756cf443eb108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a-b|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />. On the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_line\" title=\"Number line\">number line</a>, the distance between two points is the positive difference of the numbers represented by the points.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_difference&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018103413\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 13/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 349/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.661      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.661      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30456:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018103413 and revision id 238688. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}